+
+> This curated list of the best AI tools for real estate agents 2026 focuses on open source GitHub projects you can inspect, self-host, and adapt for listing copy, lead qualification, document processing, local search, and property marketing. Because direct real-estate-specific open source AI products are still limited, this list prioritizes practical GitHub repositories that real estate teams can use to build compliant, low-cost workflows around buyer intake, seller follow-up, transaction files, and media production.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
+- [License](#license)
+
+## TL;DR
+- `Flowise`, `Langflow`, and `AnythingLLM` are the fastest ways to prototype real-estate copilots for lead qualification, listing Q&A, and internal knowledge bases.
+- `Docling`, `MarkItDown`, `PaddleOCR`, `OCRmyPDF`, and `paperless-ngx` are strong picks for turning disclosures, leases, and contracts into searchable text.
+- `Haystack`, `LlamaIndex`, `LangChain`, `Qdrant`, and `Weaviate` are the most reusable building blocks for comps search, brokerage knowledge retrieval, and client-facing assistants.
+- `ComfyUI`, `InvokeAI`, `stable-diffusion-webui`, `whisper.cpp`, and `Real-ESRGAN` are the best open source options for listing media workflows, transcription, and image enhancement.
+- Gap note: truly real-estate-native open source AI repos are still sparse, so the strongest stack today is a combination of general OSS AI infrastructure plus real-estate-specific prompts, datasets, and integrations.
+
+## Why This List
+Most roundups for the best AI tools for real estate agents point to closed SaaS products, black-box pricing, and limited control over lead data. This repository takes the opposite approach: every entry must point to a public GitHub repository, expose its license, and be useful for a real estate workflow such as listing generation, CRM assistance, transaction document processing, market research, or visual marketing.
+
+Open source matters here because brokerages and independent agents often need lower operating costs, auditability, self-hosting options, and the flexibility to adapt tools around MLS rules, internal SOPs, fair housing compliance, and local market language.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
