+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best AI tools for real estate agents in 2026 if I want open source only?
+For open source only, the strongest stack usually combines a workflow builder such as `Flowise` or `Langflow`, a document pipeline such as `Docling` or `MarkItDown`, a retrieval layer such as `Qdrant`, `Weaviate`, `Haystack`, or `LlamaIndex`, and media utilities such as `whisper.cpp` or `Real-ESRGAN`. There are still few truly real-estate-native OSS projects, so the best results come from assembling a domain-specific stack from general open source AI tools.
+
+### Are there any fully open source AI tools made specifically for real estate agents?
+Very few. That is the main ecosystem gap this repository exposes honestly. Most public GitHub projects useful to real estate agents are horizontal AI tools that become real-estate-ready after you add brokerage prompts, transaction templates, neighborhood data, CRM hooks, and compliance rules.
+
+### Which open source AI repositories are best for listing descriptions and marketing copy?
+`Flowise`, `Langflow`, `LibreChat`, `AnythingLLM`, `Ollama`, and `LiteLLM` are strong options. The first four help with workflow and interfaces, while `Ollama` and `LiteLLM` make model execution and routing more practical. Add your own prompt libraries, tone guides, and approval steps for better results.
+
+### Which GitHub AI tools are best for real estate documents like disclosures, leases, and inspection reports?
+`Docling`, `MarkItDown`, `PaddleOCR`, `OCRmyPDF`, and `paperless-ngx` are the best starting points in this list. They cover structure-aware parsing, Markdown conversion, OCR, searchable PDFs, and document management. Combined with `Haystack`, `LlamaIndex`, or `LangChain`, they can support transaction QA and internal knowledge retrieval.
+
+### What open source AI tools can help a brokerage build a lead qualification chatbot?
+`Rasa`, `Flowise`, `Langflow`, `LibreChat`, `AutoGen`, and `crewAI` are the most relevant here. `Rasa` is strongest for conversation logic and structured dialogue, while the others are useful for orchestration, tool usage, and retrieval-backed assistant flows.
+
+### Can open source AI tools replace paid real estate SaaS products?
+Sometimes, but not always. Open source can replace a surprising amount of chat, retrieval, transcription, image enhancement, and internal workflow functionality. It usually does not replace MLS access, CRM data licensing, or highly vertical SaaS features by itself, so expect to combine OSS tools with your own integrations and operational rules.
+
